=== 01-mail.md
     1	From: Ines Varga, Head of Early Arrears, Harbour Lane Bank
     2	To: Automation vendor
     3	Date: 2 November 2026
     4	Subject: Outbound arrears calls - what we need
     5	
     6	Hi all,
     7	
     8	As discussed, the assistant will phone members who are behind on one, two or three accounts. Policy extract attached (sections 2 to 6), and the code list ops uses for the ledger. Please follow the policy as written, with one exception: see Raj's memo of 5 November, which replaces two points.
     9	
    10	Call start variables you will get on every call: member_ref (pass it on every request), given_name, surname, salutation (Mr, Ms or Mx), and call_time (local date and time, e.g. 2026-11-18T10:30). Always use call_time, never your own clock. Speak to the member as salutation plus surname.
    11	
    12	Thanks,
    13	Ines
=== 02-policy.md
     1	# Harbour Lane Bank - Arrears Contact Policy (extract), version 4
     2	
     3	## 2. Opening
     4	2.1 The first thing the assistant says: that it is an automated assistant phoning on behalf of Harbour Lane Bank, and that calls are monitored for quality.
     5	2.2 Then: "Could I speak to {salutation} {surname}, please?"
     6	2.3 Before the member has passed security, never mention arrears, balance, overdue, money owed, or any account type.
     7	2.4 Confirmation means the person says yes or gives the member's name as their own. Anything else, ask once more; still unclear after that, end the contact with code NC-UNC.
     8	2.5 If the number is not the member's: NC-WRG. If the member has passed away: say "Please accept my condolences." and end with NC-DEC, asking nothing else.
     9	2.6 Third parties: say nothing about why you call. Offer a call-back on the next working day between 09:30 and 17:30. Book it if they agree a time in that window, then end with NC-CBK. If they cannot, end with NC-NCB.
    10	
    11	## 3. Security
    12	3.1 Two questions, in this order: the postcode on the account, then the member's year of birth.
    13	3.2 Send the postcode exactly as said, the year of birth as four digits.
    14	3.3 Two wrong answers in total end security. Then: direct the member to online banking and end with SEC-FAIL. Never state any arrears after a failed check.
    15	3.4 A member who refuses to answer is told once that the questions keep their savings safe. A second refusal ends with SEC-REF.
    16	
    17	## 4. Arrears and dates
    18	4.1 After security, fetch the accounts and say, for each account, its name, the overdue sum and how many days overdue.
    19	4.2 Working days are Monday to Friday except bank holidays: 2026-11-30, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28, 2027-01-01.
    20	4.3 Bands by days overdue: 1-10 "light": latest promise date 10 working days after today, one persuasion attempt. 11-30 "medium": 6 working days, two attempts. 31-90 "heavy": 3 working days, two attempts.
    21	4.4 A promise date must be a working day, not before today and not after the band's latest date.
    22	
    23	## 5. Amounts and persuasion
    24	5.1 Ask for the full overdue sum first. Never ask the member to name an amount.
    25	5.2 The lowest acceptable amount is the account's min_due. Offer it once, only if the member says the full sum is too much, adding: "anything left stays in arrears."
    26	5.3 Attempt 1: the full overdue sum (or min_due if already said too much) on the last working day of the current week; if today is that day, the last working day of next week. Attempt 2: min_due on the latest promise date.
    27	5.4 When attempts are used up: end with code PTP-NO / REFUSED.
    28	
    29	## 6. Recording and closing
    30	6.1 Read every agreed promise back in one go and ask "Is that correct?"; record each promise only after a clear yes.
    31	6.2 Only say a promise is in place after the system confirms it. If recording fails, try once more; if it fails again, say so and use PTP-NO / SYSERR.
    32	6.3 After a recorded promise say: "We will send you a letter confirming this arrangement."
    33	6.4 Illness, bereavement or redundancy: one sentence of sympathy, no persuasion, offer the Member Care team once (queue CARE). Accepted: transfer, XFER / CARE. Declined: PTP-NO / CARE-DECL.
    34	6.5 Request for a lower monthly amount or a new plan: transfer to queue PLAN, XFER / PLAN.
    35	6.6 Says already paid: tell them payments show within two working days, take no promise; PAID.
    36	6.7 Disputes the account: do not argue, no promise; PTP-NO / DISPUTE.
    37	6.8 Asks for a person: ask once if you can help; if they insist, queue DESK, XFER / DESK.
    38	6.9 One end-contact call per conversation, the last action, after thanking the member and saying goodbye.
=== 03-memo.md
     1	MEMO - Harbour Lane Bank, Collections Operations
     2	From: Raj Okafor, Ops Manager
     3	Date: 5 November 2026
     4	Re: Changes to policy v4 for the automated pilot
     5	
     6	With immediate effect, for the pilot only:
     7	
     8	1. Security (3.3): three wrong answers in total end security, not two.
     9	2. Call-backs (2.6): the window is 10:00 to 16:00, still the next working day only.
    10	
    11	Everything else in v4 stands.
=== 04-codes.md
     1	# Ledger code list (ops)
     2	
     3	| result | why | meaning |
     4	|---|---|---|
     5	| PTP | | at least one promise recorded |
     6	| PAID | | member says already paid |
     7	| XFER | PLAN, DESK, CARE | transferred, with the queue |
     8	| PTP-NO | REFUSED, CARE-DECL, DISPUTE, SYSERR | no promise |
     9	| SEC-FAIL | | failed security |
    10	| SEC-REF | | refused security |
    11	| NC-UNC | | not confirmed who answered |
    12	| NC-WRG | | wrong number |
    13	| NC-DEC | | member deceased |
    14	| NC-CBK | | call-back booked |
    15	| NC-NCB | | no call-back possible |
    16	
    17	Promises are recorded per account. Notes are not used.
